  "details": "The typewriter CSS animation on the maintenance page displayed at https://wiki.vrchat.com/ can be an accessibility problem, a vestibular motion trigger for migraine or other medical symptoms.\n\nSteps to reproduce (or watch the attached video):\n\n1. Enable a reduced motion setting on your device or in your browser. In Microsoft Edge, you can emulate this with according to the instructions there: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/devtools/accessibility/reduced-motion-simulation\n\n2. Visit https://wiki.vrchat.com/ during a maintenance and check the typewriter at the bottom.\n\nExpected behavior: No blinking or vestibular motion triggers, when reduced motion setting is enabled or simulated.\n\nActual behavior: A blinking visual typewriter.\n\nOffending CSS stylesheet rules:\n\n```\n\n.t .new-output:after {\n\n    /* ... */\n\n    -webkit-animation:1.25s steps(1) infinite cursor-blink;\n\n    -moz-animation: 1.25s steps(1) infinite cursor-blink;\n\n    animation:1.25s steps(1) infinite cursor-blink;\n\n    content: ''\n\n}\n\n```\n\nAffected URLs:\n\n- https://assets.vrchat.com/www/css/under-maintainence-page.css\n\n- https://wiki.vrchat.com/ (during a maintenance)\n\nA proposed solution is to add to the CSS stylesheet:\n\n```\n\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n\n    .t .new-output:after {\n\n        -webkit-animation: none;\n\n        -moz-animation: none;\n\n        animation: none;\n\n    }\n\n}\n\n```\n\nI hereby release the above proposed changes into the public domain. This applies worldwide. If this is not legally possible: I grant any entity the right to use this work for any purpose, without any conditions, unless such conditions are required by law.\n\nAdditional info: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/At-rules/@media/prefers-reduced-motion",
